1
00:00:02,065 --> 00:00:05,027
[♪ theme music playing]

2
00:00:27,632 --> 00:00:31,053
THE HUSBAND

3
00:00:35,307 --> 00:00:36,433
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

4
00:00:36,516 --> 00:00:39,144
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

5
00:00:40,354 --> 00:00:42,230
FINAL EPISODE

6
00:00:43,315 --> 00:00:45,275
[♪ mysterious music playing]

7
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:04,461
You awake?

8
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:16,014
[inhales] Where is Ms. Kim Gyeongae?

9
00:01:19,476 --> 00:01:20,477
[snaps fingers]

10
00:01:23,105 --> 00:01:24,272
Where did you hide her?

11
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:29,986
I said I'd do her surgery.

12
00:01:33,323 --> 00:01:35,867
You're not needed anymore.
I can do the surgery.

13
00:01:36,785 --> 00:01:38,036
You?

14
00:01:39,246 --> 00:01:42,874
You can only operate
with adult stem cells.

15
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:44,918
It's likely to fail.

16
00:01:45,001 --> 00:01:46,294
[sighs]

17
00:01:46,378 --> 00:01:49,756
[Dr. Choi] I'll do the surgery,
using fetal stem cells.

18
00:01:51,675 --> 00:01:52,717
It's all in my car.

19
00:01:53,385 --> 00:01:54,386
Everything's set up.

20
00:01:56,012 --> 00:01:57,597
[Taeju] So you're saying

21
00:01:58,223 --> 00:02:00,809
you'll operate on her, with your skills?

22
00:02:04,187 --> 00:02:06,773
I don't think
you fully understand this situation.

23
00:02:07,441 --> 00:02:08,984
[chuckles] Are you that confident?

24
00:02:10,694 --> 00:02:12,571
Adult or fetal,

25
00:02:14,114 --> 00:02:16,366
can you pull off the surgery?

26
00:02:19,995 --> 00:02:21,621
[♪ tense music playing]

27
00:02:32,716 --> 00:02:34,259
[sighs]

28
00:02:54,279 --> 00:02:55,655
Where's my wife?

29
00:03:06,041 --> 00:03:11,004
THE HUSBAND

30
00:03:21,223 --> 00:03:22,265
[sighs]

31
00:03:22,849 --> 00:03:25,560
I ought to kill those scumbags.

32
00:03:37,113 --> 00:03:40,325
You trust that guy
after all that I've told you?

33
00:03:42,869 --> 00:03:44,329
I don't trust him.

34
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:48,041
I'm just weighing my options.
STYLE
::cue()

35
00:03:50,335 --> 00:03:53,922
One of you will save my wife.

36
00:04:11,314 --> 00:04:15,402
PYEONGWON FUNERAL HOME
PYEONGWON NURSING HOME

37
00:04:22,576 --> 00:04:24,160
[seat belt unbuckles]

38
00:04:24,244 --> 00:04:25,620
[phone buzzes]

39
00:05:07,996 --> 00:05:09,664
-Get out.
-[seat belt unbuckles]

40
00:05:23,303 --> 00:05:24,596
[Manhui] Wait a minute.

41
00:05:27,307 --> 00:05:30,143
You said you've got
the fetal stem cells ready.

42
00:05:32,479 --> 00:05:33,939
Go get it.

43
00:05:46,493 --> 00:05:48,161
-[trunk opens]
-[object thudding]

44
00:05:53,208 --> 00:05:54,334
It's all cultured.

45
00:05:54,417 --> 00:05:56,544
We can save your wife with--

46
00:06:01,341 --> 00:06:02,926
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

47
00:06:03,009 --> 00:06:04,344
[sighs]

48
00:06:05,178 --> 00:06:06,179
Go.

49
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,016
[door opens]

50
00:06:12,852 --> 00:06:13,853
[car chimes]

51
00:06:37,919 --> 00:06:39,921
[keys rattling]

52
00:06:42,841 --> 00:06:45,093
Honey. [gasps]

53
00:06:45,176 --> 00:06:46,428
Gyeongae.

54
00:06:46,511 --> 00:06:47,846
Honey. [panting]

55
00:06:48,596 --> 00:06:49,597
Honey.

56
00:06:49,681 --> 00:06:51,266
Gyeongae.

57
00:06:51,349 --> 00:06:53,017
[gasps] Honey.

58
00:06:53,101 --> 00:06:54,853
Yeah, it's me. I'm here.

59
00:06:54,936 --> 00:06:56,062
I'm right here.

60
00:06:56,146 --> 00:06:57,939
-Noh Manhui.
-Yes, it's me.

61
00:06:58,022 --> 00:06:59,023
[breathes shakily]

62
00:06:59,107 --> 00:07:00,692
I'm here.

63
00:07:00,775 --> 00:07:03,653
What took you so damn long?

64
00:07:03,737 --> 00:07:06,698
I told you to come back for me soon.

65
00:07:06,781 --> 00:07:08,658
I'm sorry it took so long.

66
00:07:08,742 --> 00:07:10,034
I'm here for you.

67
00:07:10,118 --> 00:07:12,162
[both breathing heavily]

68
00:07:15,373 --> 00:07:17,584
What are those people doing here?

69
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:19,085
Why did you come with them?

70
00:07:21,087 --> 00:07:22,422
[sniffs, exhales]

71
00:07:22,505 --> 00:07:24,090
You don't need him anymore, right?

72
00:07:24,591 --> 00:07:26,092
You just need me for the surgery.

73
00:07:31,723 --> 00:07:33,641
-Honey.
-[Manhui] Yeah, it's okay.

74
00:07:36,019 --> 00:07:37,562
[♪ tense music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

75
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,981
Huh?

76
00:07:40,732 --> 00:07:44,778
[syringe cap clicks, clatters]

77
00:07:47,113 --> 00:07:48,948
[cap clatters]

78
00:07:54,454 --> 00:07:56,331
[♪ music intensifies]

79
00:08:00,418 --> 00:08:01,461
[Dr. Choi] Finish him off.

80
00:08:02,086 --> 00:08:03,213
With your own hands.

81
00:08:10,845 --> 00:08:12,806
Don't you want to save your wife?

82
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,046
What… What are you doing?

83
00:08:45,130 --> 00:08:46,131
What are you doing?

84
00:08:46,214 --> 00:08:47,882
-[straining] You…
-[grunting]

85
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:50,927
[both grunting]

86
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,721
Look at this.

87
00:08:53,805 --> 00:08:55,348
SURGERY SUCCESS RATE: 13%

88
00:08:56,599 --> 00:08:59,769
You're going to save my wife
with these kinds of odds?

89
00:08:59,853 --> 00:09:02,063
-Huh? Huh?
-[grunts]

90
00:09:02,147 --> 00:09:04,315
You bastard. Huh?

91
00:09:04,399 --> 00:09:06,192
-[grunts]
-No…

92
00:09:06,276 --> 00:09:07,819
-[screams]
-[grunts]

93
00:09:09,404 --> 00:09:10,530
[gasps]

94
00:09:10,613 --> 00:09:11,990
[panting]

95
00:09:12,073 --> 00:09:13,908
[groaning, panting]

96
00:09:15,910 --> 00:09:16,953
[grunts]

97
00:09:19,372 --> 00:09:21,666
[panting]

98
00:09:23,585 --> 00:09:24,711
[sighs]

99
00:09:29,632 --> 00:09:30,633
Huh?

100
00:09:32,886 --> 00:09:34,053
Damn it.

101
00:09:36,055 --> 00:09:38,391
[panting]

102
00:09:45,148 --> 00:09:46,941
CLINICAL TRIAL REPORT
DR. CHOI CHIUNG

103
00:09:47,692 --> 00:09:49,777
Why did you stop me? Huh?

104
00:09:50,570 --> 00:09:53,031
[shouting] Why did you stop me? [panting]

105
00:09:53,698 --> 00:09:55,325
You shouldn't do this anymore.

106
00:09:57,785 --> 00:10:00,538
That guy tried to kill my wife, okay?

107
00:10:00,622 --> 00:10:04,834
He also made me kidnap yours
and tried to have you killed too!

108
00:10:05,543 --> 00:10:06,544
Yeah, I know.

109
00:10:06,628 --> 00:10:08,504
You do?

110
00:10:08,588 --> 00:10:11,382
That bastard was going to kill my wife!

111
00:10:11,883 --> 00:10:12,967
So?

112
00:10:14,469 --> 00:10:16,221
You're going to kill him now?

113
00:10:18,014 --> 00:10:19,849
That's pretty convenient.

114
00:10:21,142 --> 00:10:24,103
It's okay to kill
as long as you've got a cause, right?

115
00:10:29,108 --> 00:10:30,526
But you know what?

116
00:10:35,573 --> 00:10:37,158
I want to kill you just as much.

117
00:10:40,495 --> 00:10:41,746
Every time I look at you,

118
00:10:42,789 --> 00:10:44,290
I think of my wife.

119
00:10:44,374 --> 00:10:47,710
And how terrible it must've been
to be locked up in there, and how…

120
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,423
How painful it must have been.

121
00:10:54,717 --> 00:10:57,095
The thought alone
damn near drives me insane.

122
00:10:58,429 --> 00:10:59,597
But I won't kill you.

123
00:11:00,765 --> 00:11:02,684
And that's not because I can't.

124
00:11:10,775 --> 00:11:12,360
SURGERY SUCCESS RATE: 13%

125
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,154
Who's that from?

126
00:11:16,281 --> 00:11:17,282
Cha Myeonghui.
STYLE
::cue()

127
00:11:27,542 --> 00:11:28,793
Long time no see.

128
00:11:29,294 --> 00:11:30,295
How have you been?

129
00:11:31,546 --> 00:11:33,423
But where are you off to in such a hurry,

130
00:11:34,799 --> 00:11:35,967
Dr. Cha Myeonghui?

131
00:11:36,551 --> 00:11:38,636
Choi Chiung had me fooled as well.

132
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:42,557
I wanted to save your wife too.
I swear I mean it.

133
00:11:45,101 --> 00:11:46,102
There's

134
00:11:47,103 --> 00:11:49,147
still one thing I can do.

135
00:11:53,484 --> 00:11:56,237
[Gyeongae screaming]

136
00:11:56,321 --> 00:11:57,739
-Honey.
-[Gyeongae grunting]

137
00:11:57,822 --> 00:11:59,073
Honey.

138
00:12:00,408 --> 00:12:03,536
-Honey, are you okay?
-[screaming, grunting continues]

139
00:12:03,619 --> 00:12:06,164
Ms. Kim, can you feel your legs?

140
00:12:06,789 --> 00:12:08,374
-[Gyeongae panting]
-Can you?

141
00:12:11,002 --> 00:12:12,003
I need an answer now.

142
00:12:12,712 --> 00:12:14,005
I can't feel them.

143
00:12:16,007 --> 00:12:18,009
The tumor's compressing
her spinal cord again.

144
00:12:18,092 --> 00:12:19,385
If we leave her like this,

145
00:12:20,678 --> 00:12:23,014
she'll be paralyzed from the waist down.

146
00:12:24,932 --> 00:12:26,768
[Gyeongae groaning]

147
00:12:27,643 --> 00:12:28,978
You can save her, right?

148
00:12:30,772 --> 00:12:32,231
If we operate right now.

149
00:12:33,274 --> 00:12:35,276
And her spinal cord
needs to be reconstructed,

150
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,528
and it needs to be done now.

151
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,533
No way.

152
00:12:42,617 --> 00:12:45,119
I don't want to put my life in his hands.

153
00:12:45,203 --> 00:12:46,746
-Gyeongae.
-[Gyeongae] Honey.

154
00:12:47,997 --> 00:12:50,208
I don't want to do this anymore.

155
00:12:50,291 --> 00:12:51,709
Honey, no!

156
00:12:53,002 --> 00:12:55,963
I am not going to owe that man my life.

157
00:12:56,047 --> 00:12:57,965
It's not like that at all, okay?

158
00:12:58,633 --> 00:13:01,302
I'll owe him and I'll pay for it. Okay?

159
00:13:02,178 --> 00:13:04,639
And you just have to make it through this.

160
00:13:05,515 --> 00:13:06,516
You understand?

161
00:13:11,938 --> 00:13:16,109
Damn it, this hurts so bad.

162
00:13:16,192 --> 00:13:18,194
[pocket knife opens]

163
00:13:25,701 --> 00:13:26,869
There.

164
00:13:27,662 --> 00:13:29,122
You do the surgery.

165
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:33,793
Everything Choi Chiung put me up to,
everything I did…

166
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:36,963
I have all the evidence you need.

167
00:13:38,506 --> 00:13:39,841
Just do the surgery,

168
00:13:40,466 --> 00:13:42,552
and I'll hand over all of it
and turn myself in.

169
00:13:45,805 --> 00:13:46,806
And so…

170
00:13:48,182 --> 00:13:49,725
you better keep your word too.

171
00:13:52,645 --> 00:13:54,188
[breathing heavily]

172
00:13:55,273 --> 00:13:56,524
Yeah, I will.

173
00:13:57,567 --> 00:14:00,903
I'll do the surgery. She's a patient.

174
00:14:01,946 --> 00:14:04,031
But that doesn't mean I forgive you.

175
00:14:04,532 --> 00:14:06,033
I'm not doing it out of mercy,

176
00:14:07,201 --> 00:14:08,703
but because I'm a doctor.

177
00:14:10,371 --> 00:14:11,789
You will pay for what you did.
STYLE
::cue()

178
00:14:17,545 --> 00:14:19,088
We have to move her immediately.

179
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,883
Honey.

180
00:14:22,592 --> 00:14:25,094
-[groaning]
-Gyeongae, careful.

181
00:14:30,766 --> 00:14:33,603
[panting, groaning]

182
00:14:36,147 --> 00:14:37,523
[car chimes]

183
00:14:51,787 --> 00:14:54,040
MISSED CALLS: SEYUN

184
00:14:57,919 --> 00:14:59,253
[dialing]

185
00:14:59,337 --> 00:15:01,923
[line ringing]

186
00:15:03,466 --> 00:15:04,467
[Dr. Ko] Hello?

187
00:15:05,218 --> 00:15:06,344
Father, it's me.

188
00:15:06,427 --> 00:15:09,222
I need to perform
an emergency surgery right now.

189
00:15:09,305 --> 00:15:10,348
What?

190
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:13,059
What emergency surgery?

191
00:15:13,142 --> 00:15:14,852
What the hell are you talking about?

192
00:15:14,936 --> 00:15:18,022
I need an OR prepped with a small team
of trusted staff members.

193
00:15:18,606 --> 00:15:21,525
Wait. Who needs this emergency surgery?

194
00:15:23,945 --> 00:15:26,197
-It's Kim Gyeongae.
-What?

195
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,741
What… Why are you operating on her?

196
00:15:28,824 --> 00:15:31,327
Father, I'll fill you in
on the details afterward.

197
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:33,704
-Please just do this for me.
-[sighs]

198
00:15:34,372 --> 00:15:35,581
I understand.

199
00:15:35,665 --> 00:15:37,500
I'll have it arranged.

200
00:15:37,583 --> 00:15:39,085
Great, thank you.

201
00:15:40,336 --> 00:15:41,462
[call ends]

202
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:43,256
[dialing]

203
00:15:43,798 --> 00:15:45,466
[phone buzzes]

204
00:15:47,176 --> 00:15:49,095
-Hello?
-Hey, honey.

205
00:15:49,178 --> 00:15:50,263
Where are you right now?

206
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:52,390
Why was your phone switched off?

207
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:55,142
I'm so sorry. Something urgent came up.

208
00:15:55,768 --> 00:15:58,396
-What happened?
-Hey, Seyun.

209
00:15:58,479 --> 00:16:02,316
Uh, could you stay
over at your parents' for now?

210
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:05,069
Why would I do that?

211
00:16:09,156 --> 00:16:10,866
[inhales] Taeju.

212
00:16:11,742 --> 00:16:13,202
What's going on?

213
00:16:13,786 --> 00:16:15,371
You're not in danger again, are you?

214
00:16:15,454 --> 00:16:17,206
No, I'm not. It's nothing like that.

215
00:16:18,791 --> 00:16:21,794
[sighs] Tell me what's going on then.

216
00:16:21,877 --> 00:16:23,504
You know, it's just…

217
00:16:24,422 --> 00:16:27,842
With all that's been happening recently,
I just have this weird feeling today.

218
00:16:27,925 --> 00:16:30,678
I'd just feel more at ease
if you'd stay with your parents.

219
00:16:31,262 --> 00:16:33,347
[sighs] Okay.

220
00:16:35,641 --> 00:16:36,809
But, Taeju.

221
00:16:37,893 --> 00:16:38,894
Yeah.

222
00:16:39,478 --> 00:16:41,605
Don't try to shoulder it all alone again.

223
00:16:42,648 --> 00:16:44,150
I know by now

224
00:16:44,233 --> 00:16:47,236
that things are at their worst
when you don't say anything.

225
00:16:47,987 --> 00:16:49,238
I'll be fine.

226
00:16:51,032 --> 00:16:52,283
Okay. Bye.

227
00:16:52,992 --> 00:16:54,035
[call ends]

228
00:16:55,953 --> 00:16:56,996
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

229
00:17:02,126 --> 00:17:08,257
PYEONGWON FUNERAL HOME
PYEONGWON NURSING HOME

230
00:17:11,886 --> 00:17:15,056
EMERGENCY ROOM

231
00:17:15,139 --> 00:17:17,391
[breathing heavily]

232
00:17:20,519 --> 00:17:21,520
[grunts]

233
00:17:22,313 --> 00:17:25,024
[panting]

234
00:17:37,119 --> 00:17:38,412
Hey. She's in that car.

235
00:17:47,755 --> 00:17:49,590
[doctor 1] All right, ma'am. Here we go.

236
00:17:50,424 --> 00:17:52,051
-[Gyeongae groaning]
-[doctor 2] Careful.

237
00:17:54,011 --> 00:17:57,223
[doctor 1] Ma'am, one step at a time now.
Careful. Watch it.

238
00:17:57,306 --> 00:17:59,433
[groaning continues]

239
00:18:00,768 --> 00:18:02,353
-Here.
-[doctor 1] Lean on the bed.

240
00:18:03,562 --> 00:18:04,855
-There.
-[doctor 3] Watch your back.

241
00:18:04,939 --> 00:18:06,232
[groaning continues]

242
00:18:06,315 --> 00:18:08,234
-[doctor 3] Okay, just a bit more.
-[doctor 2] Here we go.

243
00:18:52,653 --> 00:18:53,654
[Manhui] Honey.

244
00:18:54,238 --> 00:18:56,198
You'll be all better after this surgery.

245
00:18:56,282 --> 00:18:59,160
Wait for me, okay?

246
00:18:59,785 --> 00:19:01,287
I'll be right here.

247
00:19:01,912 --> 00:19:02,913
Okay.

248
00:19:13,841 --> 00:19:15,426
[breathes shakily]

249
00:19:19,972 --> 00:19:20,973
Save her.

250
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:25,811
Please.

251
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,606
[Taeju] I'm going to do what I have to do.

252
00:19:28,689 --> 00:19:31,859
You should think long and hard
about what it is you should do too.

253
00:19:36,030 --> 00:19:39,116
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY
RESTRICTED AREA

254
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,254
[Gyeongae] I've got to say,

255
00:19:53,214 --> 00:19:55,299
we can't seem to get rid of each other.

256
00:19:58,677 --> 00:19:59,762
Isn't it funny?

257
00:20:02,556 --> 00:20:04,892
Having to save someone you hate to death

258
00:20:06,143 --> 00:20:08,521
with your own hands twice.

259
00:20:09,522 --> 00:20:10,940
But please do it.

260
00:20:12,149 --> 00:20:14,026
I want to live.

261
00:20:16,779 --> 00:20:18,572
You're a doctor.

262
00:20:22,493 --> 00:20:24,078
Ready to start anesthesia.

263
00:20:25,204 --> 00:20:26,455
[anesthesiologist] Yes, Doctor.

264
00:20:29,834 --> 00:20:32,670
[equipment hissing]
STYLE
::cue()

265
00:21:11,125 --> 00:21:13,294
[heart monitor beeping]

266
00:21:15,004 --> 00:21:16,338
[Taeju] All right, let's begin.

267
00:21:16,422 --> 00:21:17,840
Ten blade, please.

268
00:21:29,310 --> 00:21:31,228
The tumor margins are visible.

269
00:21:32,313 --> 00:21:33,480
Bipolar.

270
00:21:53,918 --> 00:21:55,169
Tumor forceps, please.

271
00:21:58,088 --> 00:22:00,007
[instruments clinking]

272
00:22:21,195 --> 00:22:22,529
[sighs]

273
00:22:25,866 --> 00:22:27,201
[sighs]

274
00:22:31,246 --> 00:22:32,623
Open the scaffold, please.

275
00:23:21,922 --> 00:23:24,216
-BP's dropping, Doctor. 85 over 55.
-[machines beeping]

276
00:23:24,967 --> 00:23:26,593
[nurse] We're seeing increased bleeding.

277
00:23:29,471 --> 00:23:30,639
[Taeju] Suction.

278
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,186
What's going on? [gasps]

279
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:39,606
[breathing shakily]

280
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,318
Bipolar.

281
00:23:45,195 --> 00:23:46,822
-Keep the suction on.
-Yes, Doctor.

282
00:23:47,531 --> 00:23:48,907
Phenylephrine.

283
00:23:48,991 --> 00:23:50,701
[anesthesiologist] Push the phenylephrine.

284
00:23:51,618 --> 00:23:52,953
[exhales]

285
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:01,587
Okay, wide open on the IV fluids.

286
00:24:02,171 --> 00:24:03,714
Get another unit of PRBCs on standby.

287
00:24:03,797 --> 00:24:04,798
[anesthesiologist] One more unit.

288
00:24:09,470 --> 00:24:10,596
Honey.

289
00:24:17,352 --> 00:24:18,854
[nurse] Bleeding is controlled.

290
00:24:19,521 --> 00:24:21,065
Vitals are stabilizing.

291
00:24:22,316 --> 00:24:25,277
-What's our total blood loss so far?
-We're past 250 ccs, Doctor.

292
00:24:29,740 --> 00:24:30,866
Okay, we're good.

293
00:24:31,658 --> 00:24:33,494
Let's continue.

294
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,413
Suture, please.
STYLE
::cue()

295
00:24:55,140 --> 00:24:58,310
SEONGJIN POLICE STATION
SAFE SEONGJIN, TRUSTED POLICE

296
00:25:00,979 --> 00:25:02,981
-Captain.
-[in English] Oh, thank you.

297
00:25:06,902 --> 00:25:08,153
[sighs]

298
00:25:09,738 --> 00:25:10,989
[in Korean] How can I…

299
00:25:11,907 --> 00:25:12,908
Captain.

300
00:25:17,830 --> 00:25:19,957
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

301
00:25:21,458 --> 00:25:22,543
Ms. Cha Myeonghui.

302
00:25:23,544 --> 00:25:24,670
I'm ready…

303
00:25:26,213 --> 00:25:28,006
to tell you everything.

304
00:25:34,847 --> 00:25:36,140
-[door opens]
-[bell chimes]

305
00:25:36,807 --> 00:25:38,600
Welcome in.

306
00:25:46,525 --> 00:25:47,776
[bottle opens]

307
00:25:51,655 --> 00:25:54,700
Oh, gosh. Excuse me.
You haven't paid for that.

308
00:25:55,409 --> 00:25:56,660
-Give me a break.
-[sighs]

309
00:25:57,995 --> 00:26:00,956
Oh, dear. Excuse me!
You have to pay first!

310
00:26:01,748 --> 00:26:06,545
My goodness. I get you're thirsty,
but you have to pay first.

311
00:26:06,628 --> 00:26:07,713
Goodness me.

312
00:26:13,260 --> 00:26:14,428
[Dr. Choi sighs]

313
00:26:21,894 --> 00:26:23,061
Go ahead. Ring me up.

314
00:26:25,189 --> 00:26:26,773
[register beeps]

315
00:26:27,608 --> 00:26:28,984
[owner] That'll be 7,300 won.

316
00:26:47,502 --> 00:26:49,421
[sighs] Hey.

317
00:26:49,504 --> 00:26:51,381
[♪ dramatic music playing]

318
00:26:52,007 --> 00:26:53,300
Let me borrow your car.

319
00:26:57,429 --> 00:26:58,639
SIWON CONVENIENCE STORE

320
00:26:58,722 --> 00:27:00,057
Please help.

321
00:27:01,058 --> 00:27:03,018
[heart monitor beeping]

322
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:07,689
Dr. Yoon, could you get
the monitoring room on the line?

323
00:27:07,773 --> 00:27:08,774
Yes, Doctor.

324
00:27:10,108 --> 00:27:11,401
You're patched in.

325
00:27:12,110 --> 00:27:13,320
[PA system beeps]

326
00:27:24,164 --> 00:27:25,582
[Taeju] Can you hear me?

327
00:27:25,666 --> 00:27:27,334
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

328
00:27:31,380 --> 00:27:33,924
I'm keeping my promise.
It's your turn now.

329
00:27:35,717 --> 00:27:38,136
The evidence you said you had on you.

330
00:27:39,179 --> 00:27:42,099
Send everything over
to Captain Jang Dosik at Seongjin PD.

331
00:27:42,766 --> 00:27:44,393
I will once you're finished.

332
00:27:45,769 --> 00:27:47,229
No, do it right now.

333
00:27:47,813 --> 00:27:49,356
Finish the surgery first.

334
00:27:53,735 --> 00:27:55,320
I think you're forgetting…

335
00:27:56,822 --> 00:27:59,282
that your wife's life
is in my hands right now.

336
00:28:02,369 --> 00:28:06,039
The longer you hesitate,
the fewer options I'm left with here.

337
00:28:07,624 --> 00:28:08,959
[Manhui] Are you

338
00:28:09,751 --> 00:28:11,294
threatening me right now?

339
00:28:11,795 --> 00:28:13,755
[Taeju] Yeah, using your exact playbook.

340
00:28:14,339 --> 00:28:18,218
Using people's fear of losing
their loved ones to control them.

341
00:28:18,802 --> 00:28:20,637
That's what you're best at.

342
00:28:31,398 --> 00:28:32,566
Send it. Right now.
STYLE
::cue()

343
00:28:48,874 --> 00:28:51,376
Have you spoken to Dr. Choi
on the phone lately?

344
00:28:53,378 --> 00:28:54,379
No.

345
00:28:55,464 --> 00:28:56,840
[Detective Oh]
So you haven't talked to him.

346
00:29:01,386 --> 00:29:03,805
Captain, we're unable
to locate Choi Chiung.

347
00:29:03,889 --> 00:29:06,016
He's not at home,
and his phone's turned off.

348
00:29:07,517 --> 00:29:08,977
[sighs]

349
00:29:09,061 --> 00:29:10,062
Keep looking.

350
00:29:10,145 --> 00:29:11,271
Yes, sir.

351
00:29:13,648 --> 00:29:15,150
[phone buzzes]

352
00:29:15,650 --> 00:29:20,113
MESSAGES
NEW MESSAGE

353
00:29:21,948 --> 00:29:23,241
What the hell?

354
00:29:24,159 --> 00:29:25,160
RECORDINGS

355
00:29:25,243 --> 00:29:27,287
[Dr. Choi]
With Kang Taeju out of the picture,

356
00:29:27,370 --> 00:29:29,331
the director will
eventually stop holding out

357
00:29:29,414 --> 00:29:31,208
and resume the project.

358
00:29:32,084 --> 00:29:34,795
[Manhui]
You're saying if we got rid of him,

359
00:29:34,878 --> 00:29:38,548
you could save my wife, right?

360
00:29:38,632 --> 00:29:39,883
[Dr. Choi] Yes.

361
00:29:39,966 --> 00:29:43,553
Get Kang Taeju out of the picture,
and I promise,

362
00:29:43,637 --> 00:29:45,889
I'll save your wife's life at all costs.

363
00:29:45,972 --> 00:29:47,682
[phone buzzes]

364
00:29:54,064 --> 00:29:55,607
WRITTEN CONFESSION
NAME: NOH MANHUI

365
00:29:55,690 --> 00:29:58,068
I, NOH MANHUI, HEREBY CONFESS
TO THE SERIES OF CRIMES…

366
00:30:06,701 --> 00:30:07,953
[sighs]

367
00:30:13,416 --> 00:30:14,584
[door opens]

368
00:30:22,425 --> 00:30:24,553
[Dr. Ko] How's Dr. Kang's surgery going?

369
00:30:25,053 --> 00:30:26,304
Is everything all right?

370
00:30:28,765 --> 00:30:31,351
Let me know if anything comes up.

371
00:30:31,852 --> 00:30:33,436
Yeah, okay.

372
00:30:34,729 --> 00:30:35,981
-[call ends]
-[door opens]

373
00:30:38,984 --> 00:30:40,652
What surgery are you talking about?

374
00:30:41,736 --> 00:30:42,821
Seyun.

375
00:30:42,904 --> 00:30:45,198
Who is Taeju operating on right now?

376
00:30:46,074 --> 00:30:47,826
Well, that's…

377
00:30:47,909 --> 00:30:48,994
Dad!

378
00:30:55,917 --> 00:30:57,002
[dialing]

379
00:30:57,085 --> 00:30:59,504
Detective Jang, it's Ko Seyun.

380
00:31:00,005 --> 00:31:02,090
[heart monitor beeping]

381
00:31:06,303 --> 00:31:07,429
I sent it.

382
00:31:25,697 --> 00:31:28,074
[breathing heavily]

383
00:31:29,993 --> 00:31:31,119
You little…

384
00:31:31,995 --> 00:31:33,330
RESTRICTED AREA

385
00:31:35,957 --> 00:31:37,918
What the hell, man?

386
00:31:38,001 --> 00:31:39,669
I did everything as you said!

387
00:31:39,753 --> 00:31:41,463
What the hell's going on?

388
00:31:42,047 --> 00:31:43,173
The surgery's over.

389
00:31:43,256 --> 00:31:45,342
[breathing shakily] What?

390
00:31:45,425 --> 00:31:47,135
The surgery is done.

391
00:31:49,304 --> 00:31:51,556
The tumor's out,
and the reconstruction's done.

392
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:53,433
Surgery was a success.

393
00:31:56,603 --> 00:31:58,104
Your wife's going to make it.

394
00:32:00,148 --> 00:32:01,233
Are you sure?

395
00:32:01,316 --> 00:32:04,527
We were already done closing her up

396
00:32:05,403 --> 00:32:07,113
before you even sent the files over.

397
00:32:10,867 --> 00:32:13,245
All right, your wife is safe now.

398
00:32:17,415 --> 00:32:19,000
So you'd better keep your word.
STYLE
::cue()

399
00:32:42,899 --> 00:32:44,192
[car chimes]

400
00:32:48,947 --> 00:32:50,865
[breathing heavily]

401
00:33:05,297 --> 00:33:06,298
Chiung.

402
00:33:07,632 --> 00:33:08,633
Ms. Ko.

403
00:33:12,137 --> 00:33:14,889
What are you doing here this early?

404
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:17,726
Something urgent came up.

405
00:33:19,561 --> 00:33:21,479
You sure you're not here to see Taeju?

406
00:33:28,153 --> 00:33:29,821
How did the surgery go?

407
00:33:34,326 --> 00:33:36,036
So he's gone and done it.

408
00:33:41,499 --> 00:33:42,792
It's Kang Taeju again.

409
00:33:46,046 --> 00:33:47,255
It's always been like this.

410
00:33:49,341 --> 00:33:51,468
He always gets to do it in the end.

411
00:33:52,802 --> 00:33:54,179
I'm the one who found them.

412
00:33:54,971 --> 00:33:56,514
I waited all that time.

413
00:33:57,182 --> 00:34:00,352
And I prepared everything. I did it all!

414
00:34:00,435 --> 00:34:01,895
[♪ dramatic music playing]

415
00:34:02,771 --> 00:34:04,773
But it's always him holding the scalpel.

416
00:34:08,610 --> 00:34:10,320
You know whose fault that is?

417
00:34:13,573 --> 00:34:14,991
It's yours, Ms. Ko.

418
00:34:18,453 --> 00:34:20,622
You're the one
who brought him to this hospital.

419
00:34:27,003 --> 00:34:28,254
[sighs]

420
00:34:31,007 --> 00:34:32,342
Yeah.

421
00:34:34,302 --> 00:34:36,221
This is all your fault, Ko Seyun.

422
00:34:46,272 --> 00:34:47,690
Chiung.

423
00:34:51,903 --> 00:34:53,405
You're out of your mind.

424
00:34:53,488 --> 00:34:54,489
No.

425
00:34:55,824 --> 00:34:57,784
I finally see things for what they are.

426
00:34:58,576 --> 00:35:00,120
Today, you

427
00:35:01,454 --> 00:35:02,580
and your husband…

428
00:35:04,791 --> 00:35:05,834
You're both dead.

429
00:35:06,543 --> 00:35:09,087
-[grunting]
-[screams]

430
00:35:10,004 --> 00:35:12,215
-[panting, grunting]
-[straining]

431
00:35:12,298 --> 00:35:13,800
[Seyun screaming]

432
00:35:14,384 --> 00:35:15,719
[Dr. Choi screams]

433
00:35:16,803 --> 00:35:19,097
[groaning, panting]

434
00:35:24,477 --> 00:35:26,688
[breathing heavily]

435
00:35:31,192 --> 00:35:32,318
[door opens]

436
00:35:33,319 --> 00:35:34,362
[elevator chimes]

437
00:35:34,446 --> 00:35:36,531
-[electronic voice] The doors are opening.
-[Dosik] Choi Chiung!

438
00:35:40,243 --> 00:35:42,787
You're not getting to my husband!

439
00:35:42,871 --> 00:35:45,206
[screams]

440
00:35:45,957 --> 00:35:48,293
-[thuds]
-[wheezing]

441
00:35:49,836 --> 00:35:51,254
-[Dosik] Ms. Ko!
-Hold him down.

442
00:35:52,005 --> 00:35:56,926
[Hyeonsu] Mr. Choi, you are under arrest
for solicitation of kidnapping and murder.

443
00:35:57,010 --> 00:35:59,053
-You have the right to stay silent…
-[Dosik] Ms. Ko!

444
00:35:59,137 --> 00:36:01,014
-…and the right to an attorney.
-[Dosik] Ms. Ko!

445
00:36:01,097 --> 00:36:03,558
-Requesting medical support!
-[Hyeonsu] If you can't afford one,

446
00:36:03,641 --> 00:36:05,393
one will be provided for you.
STYLE
::cue()

447
00:36:32,128 --> 00:36:33,296
Gyeongae.

448
00:36:35,673 --> 00:36:36,800
It's all over.

449
00:37:41,781 --> 00:37:42,907
What are you doing?

450
00:37:46,202 --> 00:37:47,704
Put the knife down.

451
00:37:48,288 --> 00:37:49,289
She's alive.

452
00:37:50,582 --> 00:37:51,833
That's all that matters.

453
00:37:52,709 --> 00:37:54,002
I sent over the files.

454
00:37:54,502 --> 00:37:56,671
They should have everything they need now.

455
00:37:59,007 --> 00:38:00,008
One thing.

456
00:38:00,633 --> 00:38:02,427
My wife's name isn't on there.

457
00:38:06,222 --> 00:38:08,308
I'm taking all the blame and ending this.

458
00:38:13,897 --> 00:38:14,898
Put it down.

459
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:17,317
We can talk this out.

460
00:38:20,612 --> 00:38:21,946
Stay away.

461
00:38:27,118 --> 00:38:28,828
If you die, what about your wife?

462
00:38:31,331 --> 00:38:34,709
You think she'll be happy without you
as if none of this ever happened?

463
00:38:35,710 --> 00:38:37,003
She'll manage.

464
00:38:37,086 --> 00:38:39,714
No, stop lying to yourself.
You're just running away.

465
00:38:40,590 --> 00:38:42,258
You're taking the easy way out.

466
00:38:43,927 --> 00:38:47,180
You killed all those people,
claiming it was to save your wife,

467
00:38:47,764 --> 00:38:51,517
and now you're using her
as an excuse to kill yourself?

468
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:57,440
Hey, look.

469
00:38:59,567 --> 00:39:01,069
You're being a coward.

470
00:39:03,905 --> 00:39:05,490
You're being selfish.

471
00:39:08,368 --> 00:39:09,827
If you die here…

472
00:39:12,789 --> 00:39:16,125
your wife has to take the fall
for all your crimes.

473
00:39:16,709 --> 00:39:17,710
Then what?

474
00:39:18,711 --> 00:39:20,338
What am I supposed to…

475
00:39:21,422 --> 00:39:23,675
What am I supposed to do? Huh?

476
00:39:25,635 --> 00:39:26,678
Live.

477
00:39:30,098 --> 00:39:31,432
And take accountability.

478
00:39:34,143 --> 00:39:35,228
I can't.

479
00:39:36,813 --> 00:39:38,356
I can't do that to my Gyeongae.

480
00:39:39,941 --> 00:39:43,069
I can't let her live
her whole life as a criminal.

481
00:39:43,820 --> 00:39:45,279
Absolutely no way.

482
00:39:48,324 --> 00:39:49,325
I'm sorry, honey.

483
00:39:50,326 --> 00:39:51,619
[both grunt]

484
00:39:51,703 --> 00:39:53,329
Let go.

485
00:39:54,789 --> 00:39:55,999
I said let go!

486
00:39:56,082 --> 00:39:59,585
I can't let you and your wife
get off that easy.

487
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:03,006
Live and pay for your crimes.

488
00:40:03,798 --> 00:40:06,551
[Taeju groaning]

489
00:40:10,430 --> 00:40:12,432
Noh Manhui, drop the knife! Get him!

490
00:40:13,391 --> 00:40:15,935
Mr. Kang! Come here!

491
00:40:16,019 --> 00:40:20,231
Mr. Noh, you're under arrest
for kidnapping and murder.

492
00:40:20,314 --> 00:40:22,608
You have the right to remain silent

493
00:40:22,692 --> 00:40:24,569
and the right to an attorney.

494
00:40:24,652 --> 00:40:29,282
If you can't afford one,
one will be provided for you.
STYLE
::cue()

495
00:40:39,709 --> 00:40:41,169
[sighs]

496
00:40:48,926 --> 00:40:50,261
Mr. Kang, your hand…

497
00:40:55,391 --> 00:40:56,893
Choi Chiung has been arrested.

498
00:40:56,976 --> 00:40:58,311
But…

499
00:40:59,437 --> 00:41:01,189
Ms. Ko is seriously injured.

500
00:41:14,911 --> 00:41:19,373
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY
RESTRICTED AREA

501
00:41:21,793 --> 00:41:23,169
[sobs]

502
00:41:23,252 --> 00:41:25,129
Where have you been?

503
00:41:26,547 --> 00:41:28,549
I said, where have you been?

504
00:41:32,095 --> 00:41:34,430
Where have you been?

505
00:41:46,234 --> 00:41:48,736
[doctor] Any more delay, and she could be
permanently paralyzed.

506
00:41:48,820 --> 00:41:50,071
We're operating right now.

507
00:41:50,655 --> 00:41:52,240
-Let's get her under.
-[anesthesiologist] Yes, Doctor.

508
00:42:03,126 --> 00:42:05,461
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

509
00:42:07,505 --> 00:42:08,589
Honey.

510
00:42:11,175 --> 00:42:12,593
I'm not late this time, am I?

511
00:42:29,026 --> 00:42:30,778
Okay, let's get started.

512
00:42:31,571 --> 00:42:32,780
Blade, please.

513
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:48,421
[anchor] New developments in
the kidnapping at a major local hospital.

514
00:42:48,504 --> 00:42:51,048
The full story behind the kidnapping
and attempted murder

515
00:42:51,132 --> 00:42:53,092
at a major hospital
is now coming to light.

516
00:42:53,176 --> 00:42:54,844
[reporter 1]
Is it true that you planned the crime?

517
00:42:54,927 --> 00:42:57,471
-[reporter 2] Any words for the victims?
-[reporter 3] When did you hatch the plan?

518
00:42:57,555 --> 00:42:59,932
-[reporter 4] Do you admit to the crime?
-[reporter 5] Will you plead guilty?

519
00:43:00,016 --> 00:43:01,309
[reporter 4] Do you have anything to say?

520
00:43:01,392 --> 00:43:02,810
-[Detective Oh] Coming through.
-[reporter 6] Any comments?

521
00:43:02,894 --> 00:43:03,895
[Detective Oh] Please make way.

522
00:43:03,978 --> 00:43:07,607
[anchor] Police have identified
the hospital's vice director,

523
00:43:07,690 --> 00:43:11,277
Choi, as the one who planned
and orchestrated the crime.

524
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:14,614
However, Choi has reportedly
denied all allegations.

525
00:43:16,365 --> 00:43:18,659
-He's coming out!
-There he is!

526
00:43:19,827 --> 00:43:21,287
[reporter 7] Any comments on the matter?

527
00:43:23,581 --> 00:43:26,417
[anchor] Investigators say Noh Manhui,
who carried out the crime,

528
00:43:26,500 --> 00:43:30,671
handed over a written confession
and audio recordings detailing the offense

529
00:43:30,755 --> 00:43:32,632
to police before his arrest.

530
00:43:32,715 --> 00:43:35,801
Noh insists he acted alone
and strongly denies that his wife,

531
00:43:35,885 --> 00:43:37,970
Kim, had any part in it.

532
00:43:38,054 --> 00:43:40,932
However, police believe
there's evidence that Kim conspired

533
00:43:41,015 --> 00:43:43,476
in the kidnapping and false imprisonment,

534
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:46,896
and plan to refer her case
to the prosecutors first.

535
00:43:46,979 --> 00:43:50,358
NOH MANHUI CLAIMS HIS WIFE IS INNOCENT

536
00:44:05,581 --> 00:44:07,833
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
FUND DONATION AGREEMENT

537
00:44:10,628 --> 00:44:12,672
[Seyun] We have to make right what we can.

538
00:44:13,464 --> 00:44:15,716
And you have to be the one to do it.

539
00:44:16,550 --> 00:44:17,551
DIRECTOR KO DONGCHAN

540
00:44:19,971 --> 00:44:22,848
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

541
00:44:22,932 --> 00:44:26,018
DISTINGUISHED SERVICE AWARD
SPINE CLINICAL RESEARCH FOUNDATION

542
00:44:26,102 --> 00:44:28,813
[anchor 2] Dr. Ko Dongchan, director
of Woori Together Medical Center,

543
00:44:28,896 --> 00:44:30,690
turned himself in to police this morning.

544
00:44:30,773 --> 00:44:34,527
Ko reportedly acknowledged responsibility
for the illegal medical practices

545
00:44:34,610 --> 00:44:38,864
and stated that he would fully
cooperate with the police investigation.

546
00:44:38,948 --> 00:44:43,327
Dr. Ko, a leading figure
in spinal neurosurgery,

547
00:44:43,411 --> 00:44:48,541
is accused of illegally obtaining
stem cells from aborted fetuses

548
00:44:48,624 --> 00:44:50,042
and using them in surgeries

549
00:44:50,126 --> 00:44:51,794
-to improve the success rate…
-[phone buzzing]

550
00:44:51,877 --> 00:44:56,340
…of a highly anticipated spinal cord
reconstruction clinical trial.

551
00:44:57,883 --> 00:44:59,093
Yes, hello?
STYLE
::cue()

552
00:45:02,054 --> 00:45:04,724
I'm sorry to bother you again.

553
00:45:05,433 --> 00:45:06,642
It's no problem.

554
00:45:06,726 --> 00:45:09,895
Do you remember the video
you talked to us about?

555
00:45:09,979 --> 00:45:12,315
The video of your husband
you saw in captivity.

556
00:45:14,108 --> 00:45:15,192
Yes.

557
00:45:15,276 --> 00:45:16,569
We recovered what seems to be

558
00:45:16,652 --> 00:45:19,071
the original file
from the perp's computer.

559
00:45:19,572 --> 00:45:22,658
We just need you to confirm
if it's the same as the one you saw.

560
00:45:22,742 --> 00:45:23,743
Okay.

561
00:45:28,914 --> 00:45:30,750
I'll give you a moment.

562
00:45:35,296 --> 00:45:36,756
[door opens]

563
00:45:38,424 --> 00:45:39,842
[door closes]

564
00:45:41,093 --> 00:45:43,095
[Manhui] Sir, did you call for a driver?

565
00:45:44,305 --> 00:45:47,641
[Taeju] I feel like I made the call
a second ago. You got here so quickly.

566
00:45:47,725 --> 00:45:51,729
[Manhui] Well, I just happened to be
in the area, so I got here fast.

567
00:45:57,985 --> 00:46:00,905
You must be exhausted, sir. Oh, here.

568
00:46:01,781 --> 00:46:04,325
I got this for myself,
but you can have it.

569
00:46:06,035 --> 00:46:08,412
Oh, thanks. I appreciate it.

570
00:46:15,503 --> 00:46:16,629
[coughs]

571
00:46:17,254 --> 00:46:18,631
[grunts]

572
00:46:20,549 --> 00:46:22,134
[inhales]

573
00:46:31,811 --> 00:46:32,853
Hey…

574
00:46:33,604 --> 00:46:34,605
[Manhui] Yeah?

575
00:46:36,023 --> 00:46:37,691
[Taeju] Have you ever…

576
00:46:39,527 --> 00:46:41,070
lost a loved one?

577
00:46:41,153 --> 00:46:42,696
[chuckles]

578
00:46:42,780 --> 00:46:45,699
Well, yeah, of course.
But I mean, who hasn't?

579
00:46:45,783 --> 00:46:48,452
No. Not like that.

580
00:46:49,912 --> 00:46:51,080
Like…

581
00:46:53,499 --> 00:46:56,710
Have you lost anyone that you truly love?

582
00:47:01,048 --> 00:47:02,716
I'm always trying my absolute best

583
00:47:03,592 --> 00:47:05,094
not to let that happen.

584
00:47:09,473 --> 00:47:10,558
You see…

585
00:47:14,228 --> 00:47:15,855
I've lost my little girl.

586
00:47:19,483 --> 00:47:21,902
I should have been there for my wife.

587
00:47:24,864 --> 00:47:27,199
But I didn't have the guts
to tell her the truth.

588
00:47:28,784 --> 00:47:30,119
[inhales] Hmm.

589
00:47:31,203 --> 00:47:32,872
So I couldn't be there.

590
00:47:33,706 --> 00:47:35,124
[Manhui] I see.

591
00:47:36,667 --> 00:47:37,918
Go on.

592
00:47:38,002 --> 00:47:40,796
I want to tell my wife
the truth about everything,

593
00:47:41,755 --> 00:47:45,092
but I worry she might break down
if she found out everything.

594
00:47:47,136 --> 00:47:49,388
I can't bring myself to say anything.

595
00:47:50,806 --> 00:47:52,141
[Manhui] But I mean,

596
00:47:53,142 --> 00:47:56,437
don't you think things would get better
if you just talked to her about it?

597
00:47:57,021 --> 00:47:59,190
No.

598
00:48:01,066 --> 00:48:02,610
[exhales]

599
00:48:03,402 --> 00:48:08,199
I can't let her live with the consequences
of the choices that I've made.

600
00:48:09,492 --> 00:48:11,452
But you know,

601
00:48:12,286 --> 00:48:13,579
there's a limit

602
00:48:14,330 --> 00:48:18,459
to how much you can lie.

603
00:48:21,962 --> 00:48:23,047
So…

604
00:48:26,383 --> 00:48:29,220
I said we should get divorced.

605
00:48:31,388 --> 00:48:32,598
Oh, no.

606
00:48:34,433 --> 00:48:36,018
But she said she didn't want to.

607
00:48:36,101 --> 00:48:37,102
Well…

608
00:48:40,314 --> 00:48:41,607
She said she'd never do it.

609
00:48:43,651 --> 00:48:44,735
Why's that?

610
00:48:45,236 --> 00:48:46,487
Because it's what I want.

611
00:48:46,987 --> 00:48:48,197
[sighs]

612
00:48:49,114 --> 00:48:52,535
She doesn't want to
give me anything I want.

613
00:48:54,495 --> 00:48:56,664
I'm all out of options now.

614
00:48:58,916 --> 00:49:00,584
Anyway, that being said…

615
00:49:04,421 --> 00:49:06,715
I want you to get rid of my wife.

616
00:49:06,799 --> 00:49:09,218
What? What did you say?

617
00:49:09,301 --> 00:49:10,844
I'll pay you, okay?

618
00:49:11,679 --> 00:49:14,056
I'll pay you 300… No.

619
00:49:16,058 --> 00:49:18,686
I'll pay you 500 million won. So please.

620
00:49:21,105 --> 00:49:25,442
So you want me to get rid of your wife?

621
00:49:27,278 --> 00:49:29,280
Seyun could…
STYLE
::cue()

622
00:49:35,536 --> 00:49:39,331
She could never be happy
as long as she's with me.

623
00:49:40,291 --> 00:49:41,375
So…

624
00:49:43,419 --> 00:49:45,087
I want you…

625
00:49:49,967 --> 00:49:51,760
to take my wife

626
00:49:53,012 --> 00:49:54,555
out of my life.

627
00:50:00,936 --> 00:50:04,106
So she won't be haunted by the truth…

628
00:50:09,695 --> 00:50:12,406
or be lonely because of all my lies.

629
00:50:12,489 --> 00:50:13,574
I just…

630
00:50:14,700 --> 00:50:16,035
[inhales]

631
00:50:16,827 --> 00:50:19,038
…I want her to stay in the dark…

632
00:50:26,462 --> 00:50:27,838
and disappear…

633
00:50:27,921 --> 00:50:29,465
[sniffles]

634
00:50:30,507 --> 00:50:32,426
…from my life.

635
00:50:38,349 --> 00:50:41,560
The further away she stays from me…

636
00:50:47,900 --> 00:50:51,153
the happier she would be in life.

637
00:50:55,449 --> 00:50:56,575
[sighs]

638
00:51:23,268 --> 00:51:24,478
[footsteps approaching]

639
00:51:31,485 --> 00:51:32,903
Did you get it checked out?

640
00:51:34,655 --> 00:51:35,698
Yeah.

641
00:51:36,532 --> 00:51:37,533
What did they say?

642
00:51:38,534 --> 00:51:42,287
To keep going to therapy. They said
it should be back to normal soon.

643
00:51:42,371 --> 00:51:43,831
And your work?

644
00:51:44,873 --> 00:51:46,458
Can you still do surgeries?

645
00:51:52,798 --> 00:51:53,799
I see.

646
00:51:55,175 --> 00:51:56,260
[sighs]

647
00:51:57,720 --> 00:51:59,471
It's fine. I'll be fine.

648
00:51:59,555 --> 00:52:01,640
Stop saying you're fine.

649
00:52:02,266 --> 00:52:03,851
This is clearly not fine.

650
00:52:03,934 --> 00:52:05,769
I know how much it means to…

651
00:52:06,770 --> 00:52:08,272
I mean it, I'm fine.

652
00:52:09,565 --> 00:52:11,233
I can move it and all.

653
00:52:11,984 --> 00:52:12,985
That's what matters.

654
00:52:13,068 --> 00:52:14,319
[sighs]

655
00:52:16,155 --> 00:52:17,656
You're always like this.

656
00:52:21,034 --> 00:52:23,996
It wouldn't have gotten this bad
if you'd gotten surgery right away.

657
00:52:32,129 --> 00:52:33,380
I watched…

658
00:52:35,382 --> 00:52:36,383
that video of you.

659
00:52:44,516 --> 00:52:46,059
I finally get it.

660
00:52:46,935 --> 00:52:48,979
How you must have felt at the time.

661
00:52:51,023 --> 00:52:53,442
You didn't want to get rid of me.

662
00:52:55,527 --> 00:52:57,988
You wanted to protect me.

663
00:52:59,948 --> 00:53:01,533
But that made things clearer for me.

664
00:53:04,328 --> 00:53:06,163
We'll always be like this.

665
00:53:08,499 --> 00:53:11,126
You'll hide things to protect me,

666
00:53:11,210 --> 00:53:13,504
and I'll be left in the dark and get hurt.

667
00:53:17,591 --> 00:53:19,593
That's why I'm going to let go of you.

668
00:53:25,349 --> 00:53:26,558
Let's get divorced.

669
00:53:28,644 --> 00:53:30,354
[♪ sad music playing]

670
00:53:33,524 --> 00:53:35,025
It's not your fault, though.

671
00:53:39,571 --> 00:53:40,572
I know.

672
00:53:42,616 --> 00:53:44,284
And it's not your fault, either.

673
00:53:47,955 --> 00:53:49,581
The way we love each other…

674
00:53:52,167 --> 00:53:53,710
is just very different.
STYLE
::cue()

675
00:53:58,882 --> 00:54:00,843
KANG TAEJU
NEUROSURGERY CLINIC

676
00:54:00,926 --> 00:54:02,386
-[Taeju] Come in.
-[door opens]

677
00:54:02,469 --> 00:54:03,679
CONSULTATION ROOM

678
00:54:03,762 --> 00:54:06,431
Have you been doing
the exercise I taught you last time?

679
00:54:07,099 --> 00:54:10,269
I did, but it just hurt more.

680
00:54:10,352 --> 00:54:11,353
Pardon?

681
00:54:11,937 --> 00:54:13,480
Well, that's why you have to do it.

682
00:54:13,564 --> 00:54:17,067
My goodness, you and your nagging.

683
00:54:17,150 --> 00:54:18,986
That's what you're here for, isn't it?

684
00:54:20,779 --> 00:54:22,698
Make sure to receive
physical therapy, okay?

685
00:54:24,324 --> 00:54:27,494
Grandma, you have to
actually do it this time.

686
00:54:28,245 --> 00:54:30,205
All right. [groans]

687
00:54:31,373 --> 00:54:33,041
-[grandchild] Thank you, Doctor.
-Okay, bye.

688
00:54:33,542 --> 00:54:34,710
Take care, ma'am.

689
00:54:36,003 --> 00:54:37,588
-[chuckles]
-[door closes]

690
00:54:41,425 --> 00:54:42,593
[sighs]

691
00:55:04,239 --> 00:55:06,533
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

692
00:55:07,117 --> 00:55:08,118
[mother] There it is.

693
00:55:09,244 --> 00:55:11,246
-Here.
-Go on.

694
00:55:12,331 --> 00:55:15,626
Why don't you come by more often?

695
00:55:16,335 --> 00:55:18,211
How are things over there?

696
00:55:19,212 --> 00:55:21,048
Don't you get lonely?

697
00:55:21,131 --> 00:55:22,591
No, it's good.

698
00:55:22,674 --> 00:55:24,760
You know, the patients are nice.

699
00:55:24,843 --> 00:55:26,803
It's nice and quiet.

700
00:55:26,887 --> 00:55:28,180
[Taeyeong] Geez.

701
00:55:28,263 --> 00:55:31,516
Stop saying it's all good.
Mom's clearly worried about you.

702
00:55:32,267 --> 00:55:34,102
-When will you grow up? [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

703
00:55:34,186 --> 00:55:35,812
Oh, hey, Mom. This is for you.

704
00:55:35,896 --> 00:55:37,064
What's all this?

705
00:55:37,773 --> 00:55:41,068
You seem to get worse with every checkup.
Make sure you take these.

706
00:55:41,610 --> 00:55:42,944
[gasps]

707
00:55:43,028 --> 00:55:46,531
I was actually worried
because my numbers keep dropping.

708
00:55:46,615 --> 00:55:50,118
You don't want a fracture
or a broken bone.

709
00:55:50,202 --> 00:55:52,871
A lot of patients come in
after falling accidents.

710
00:55:53,914 --> 00:55:56,166
-I got you a box, too.
-Really?

711
00:55:56,917 --> 00:55:59,461
I see you've actually grown up. [chuckles]

712
00:55:59,961 --> 00:56:02,839
I mean, it's about time
I took care of myself.

713
00:56:02,923 --> 00:56:06,051
[mother] Okay, why don't we…

714
00:56:06,843 --> 00:56:11,056
Yeah, let's take one together.

715
00:56:11,139 --> 00:56:12,391
-Yeah?
-Here, take one.

716
00:56:12,474 --> 00:56:13,892
-Okay.
-[chuckles]

717
00:56:13,975 --> 00:56:15,602
-You too.
-Wow, me too?

718
00:56:15,686 --> 00:56:17,020
Yes.

719
00:56:17,104 --> 00:56:18,146
[liquid pouring]

720
00:56:20,649 --> 00:56:21,650
There.

721
00:56:22,734 --> 00:56:24,611
All right, let's take it.

722
00:56:24,695 --> 00:56:26,321
-[giggling] Here's to our health!
-[chuckles]

723
00:56:26,405 --> 00:56:28,156
-To our health!
-To our health!

724
00:56:32,661 --> 00:56:33,787
[Taeyeong] Goodness.

725
00:56:34,746 --> 00:56:36,581
Oh, welcome.

726
00:56:36,665 --> 00:56:37,666
-[guest] Yeah, hi.
-This way.

727
00:56:37,749 --> 00:56:38,834
Okay.

728
00:56:42,421 --> 00:56:45,340
So, are you in touch at all?

729
00:56:46,258 --> 00:56:48,427
Do you hear from her?

730
00:56:50,554 --> 00:56:52,139
I'm sure she's doing fine.

731
00:56:53,515 --> 00:56:54,641
[sighs]

732
00:56:56,768 --> 00:57:00,105
You know, Mom,
a lot of women do come to see me.

733
00:57:00,188 --> 00:57:01,189
What?

734
00:57:01,815 --> 00:57:02,858
It's true.

735
00:57:03,859 --> 00:57:05,944
It's just that
they're a bit older than you.

736
00:57:06,695 --> 00:57:09,614
-They mostly come in with knee pain.
-[chuckles]

737
00:57:09,698 --> 00:57:12,868
Goodness, you silly boy.

738
00:57:13,702 --> 00:57:16,997
Well, it's good to see you
make jokes and laugh now.

739
00:57:19,166 --> 00:57:20,959
[sighs] My goodness.
STYLE
::cue()

740
00:57:56,369 --> 00:57:58,205
KANG HAYUN
MAY 20, 2022 - JANUARY 28, 2025

741
00:57:58,288 --> 00:58:00,248
Hey, Hayun. Daddy's here.

742
00:58:02,167 --> 00:58:03,585
How have you been?

743
00:58:05,670 --> 00:58:08,715
WE WILL REMEMBER YOU
LOVE YOU, SWEETHEART

744
00:58:13,595 --> 00:58:14,846
[coughs]

745
00:58:30,278 --> 00:58:31,363
How have you been?

746
00:58:32,155 --> 00:58:33,156
Good.

747
00:58:34,950 --> 00:58:35,951
That's good.

748
00:58:37,953 --> 00:58:39,037
What about you?

749
00:58:42,040 --> 00:58:43,959
I'm getting there.

750
00:59:02,602 --> 00:59:04,020
I'm going to take a walk.

751
00:59:06,982 --> 00:59:07,983
Okay.

752
00:59:11,862 --> 00:59:13,530
Can I walk with you?

753
00:59:16,616 --> 00:59:17,617
Sure.

754
00:59:17,701 --> 00:59:20,078
[♪ "Us, Now" playing]

755
00:59:50,984 --> 00:59:55,822
THE HUSBAND

756
01:01:16,987 --> 01:01:19,948
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING THE HUSBAND

757
01:01:21,241 --> 01:01:23,243
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

